---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TrustHero from "../components/TrustHero.astro";
import { siteUrl } from "../content";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Terms of Service - Claude Model Insights",
  description:
    "Terms of service for claudeopusmodels.com covering usage rules, intellectual property, and limitations.",
  url: `${siteUrl}/terms/`,
  datePublished: "2026-05-09",
  dateModified: "2026-05-09",
  inLanguage: "en-US",
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website`,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Claude Model Insights"
  description="Terms of service for claudeopusmodels.com. Usage rules, intellectual property, disclaimers, and limitations of liability. Last updated May 2026."
  path="/terms/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <TrustHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of Service"
    subtitle="Usage rules, intellectual property, disclaimers, and limitations of liability for Claude Model Insights."
    accent="#8B7355"
    meta="Effective: May 9, 2026 · Last Updated: May 9, 2026"
  />

  <article class="trust-page">
    <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing or using claudeopusmodels.com ("the Site"), you agree to
      be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you don't agree with
      any part of these Terms, please don't use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
    <p>
      Claude Model Insights is an informational blog and publication
      covering Claude AI models, vibe coding, and AI-assisted development.
      We provide articles, tutorials, comparisons, and guides. All content
      is free to read.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're an independent publication. We aren't affiliated with, endorsed
      by, or officially connected to Anthropic, PBC.
    </p>

    <h2>3. User Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16 years old to use this Site. By using the
      Site, you represent that you meet this age requirement.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>When using our Site, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the Site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable law</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to our systems, servers, or networks</li>
      <li>Scrape, crawl, or use automated tools to extract content without our written permission</li>
      <li>Reproduce, distribute, or republish our content without attribution and a link back to the original article</li>
      <li>Upload or transmit viruses, malware, or other harmful code</li>
      <li>Interfere with the Site's operation or other users' experience</li>
      <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      All content on claudeopusmodels.com, including articles, graphics,
      logos, images, and code examples, is owned by Claude Model Insights
      or used under license. This content is protected by copyright and
      other intellectual property laws.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What you can do:</strong> You may read, share links to, and
      quote brief excerpts (under 200 words) from our articles for
      non-commercial purposes, provided you include clear attribution and a
      link to the original article.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What you can't do:</strong> You can't republish full
      articles, use our content in commercial products, train AI models on
      our content without permission, or remove copyright notices.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Code Examples and Technical Content</h2>
    <p>
      Code examples provided in our tutorials are offered for educational
      purposes. You're free to use code snippets in your own projects
      (commercial or non-commercial) without attribution.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, we provide code "as is" without warranties. We're not
      responsible for any issues that arise from implementing code examples
      from our tutorials. Always review AI-generated code before deploying
      it to production, especially for applications handling sensitive data.
    </p>

    <h2>7. User Communications</h2>
    <p>
      When you contact us through our contact form or email, you grant us
      permission to use your feedback, suggestions, and ideas without
      restriction or compensation. We won't publicly share your personal
      information from communications without your consent.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
    <p>
      THE SITE AND ALL CONTENT ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE"
      WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. WE DISCLAIM ALL
      WARRANTIES INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
      MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
      NON-INFRINGEMENT.
    </p>
    <p>We don't warrant that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The Site will be uninterrupted, secure, or error-free</li>
      <li>Content will be accurate, complete, or current at all times</li>
      <li>Errors or defects will be corrected</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      AI tools and pricing change frequently. Information accurate on the
      date of publication may become outdated. We update articles
      periodically but can't guarantee every detail reflects the latest
      state of every product mentioned.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, CLAUDE MODEL
      INSIGHTS, ITS OWNER, AND CONTRIBUTORS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY
      INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES
